===Etymology===
{{named-after|en|occ=neurologists|nat=German|Hans Gerhard Creutzfeldt|born=1885|died=1964|wplink==}} and {{named-after|en|Alfons Maria Jakob|alt=|wplink==|born=1884|died=1931}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=Creutzfeldt-Jakob [[disease]]|-}}

# {{lb|en|disease|neurology}} A [[rare]], [[progressive]], [[fatal]] [[disease]] of the [[nervous system]], characterized by [[dementia]] and loss of [[muscle]] [[control]]. It is a [[prion disease]], apparently transmissible from animals to humans by eating infected tissue, as well as from tissue interchanges among humans (e.g. corneal transplants, blood transfusions).
#: {{syn|en|CJD|q1=abbreviation}}

